# Froyo Deal Tracker scheduled jobs (LINUX / cron).
# On macOS use launchd instead - see ops/com.froyo.*.plist and docs/SETUP.md
# ("Scheduling on macOS"). cron does not fire while the laptop is asleep and does
# not catch up missed runs; launchd's StartCalendarInterval does fire on wake.
# This crontab is the Linux (always-on server) path.
# Install with:  crontab ops/crontab
# Replace REPO below with the absolute path to this checkout.
# Each job cd's into the repo so python-dotenv finds .env for DATABASE_URL and
# GEMINI_API_KEY. Output is appended to logs/ (gitignored).

# Phase 6: daily website scrape, then extract new captures into pending deals.
15 3 * * * cd REPO && .venv/bin/python -m ingest.scrape && .venv/bin/python -m ingest.extract >> logs/scrape.log 2>&1

# Phase 8: expire past-dated approved deals nightly (after the scrape/extract).
30 3 * * * cd REPO && .venv/bin/python -m ingest.expire_deals >> logs/jobs.log 2>&1

# Auto-merge duplicate deals nightly (after expire), on approved AND pending so the
# review queue shows one canonical row per promo. Canonical = approved-over-pending
# then earliest id; supersedes the rest (status unchanged). Gates on the duplicate
# scorer, not model confidence; never merges null-value freebies. --commit applies
# (drop it for a dry-run preview). Every merge is logged to jobs.log.
35 3 * * * cd REPO && .venv/bin/python -m ingest.merge_dupes --commit >> logs/jobs.log 2>&1

# Phase 8: reverify approved deals weekly (Monday 04:00). Confirms the source
# still carries the offer and bumps last_verified; does not re-extract.
0 4 * * 1 cd REPO && .venv/bin/python -m ingest.reverify >> logs/jobs.log 2>&1

# Instagram scrape, 2x daily (morning/evening). The capture source itself is
# private and not included in this repository, so this line is a no-op here: the
# runner writes nothing and exits non-zero. Left in place because it is part of
# the schedule the pipeline is built around.
30 8,18 * * * cd REPO && .venv/bin/python -m ingest.scrape_instagram >> logs/instagram.log 2>&1
